      "location": "Statement",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The cited definition says a map f:X→Y is nullhomotopic when it is homotopic to a constant map, with no relative-endpoint condition. Thus γ(s)=exp(2πis) in Ω=C× is nullhomotopic as its displayed I→C× map via H(s,t)=exp(2πi(1-t)s), but f(z)=1/z is holomorphic on Ω and ∫γ f(z)dz=2πi≠0. The proof's claim that closedness makes such a homotopy endpoint-fixed is not licensed by the cited definition.",
