      "evidence": "Step 1.1 says that each contour γj in an arbitrary cycle Γ=Σnjγj is closed. The cited definition def-complex-chain-and-cycle expressly says: “Cycles are more general than lists of closed contours,” and gives two nonclosed contours with common endpoints and coefficients +1 and −1 as a cycle. Thus the fundamental-group hypothesis and the cited closed-contour corollary cannot be applied termwise as written.",
