      "evidence": "The asserted 1↔2 bridge cites lem-null-homology-implies-connected-spherical-complement. Its step 1.1 claims that, for a component K of a disconnected spherical complement, “the disjoint set (C\\Ω)\\K is closed” and hence has positive distance from K. This is false for components of a closed set: with Ω=C\\C for a compact perfect Cantor set C⊂R, each K={x}⊂C is a component but d(K,C\\K)=0. Therefore the cited proof does not establish the reverse implication used here.",
